@cc ===========================================================================
@cc Build CHATLIB and its test program, SEPARATELY, and link them.
@cc
@cc THE POINT OF THIS FILE IS HOW LITTLE IT DOES. Two small sources compile in
@cc seconds, where the full client takes about twenty minutes - so a change to
@cc the wire format can be checked before anything large is built at all.
@cc
@cc Run it with   @MODE CHATTS:MODE,,
@cc then          @CHATTS
@cc ===========================================================================

@cc --- clear the old build; NO SUCH FILE NAME on a first run is expected -----
@DELETE-FILE CHATTS:PROG
@DELETE-FILE CHATLIB:BRF
@DELETE-FILE CHATTST:BRF
@DELETE-FILE CHATLIB:LIST
@DELETE-FILE CHATTST:LIST

@cc --- the library, on its own ----------------------------------------------
@cc Quoting: no quotes means the file must already exist, "quotes" means create.
@PLANC-100-F00
COMPILE CHATLIB:PLNC,"CHATLIB:LIST","CHATLIB"
EXIT

@cc --- the test program, on its own -----------------------------------------
@PLANC-100-F00
COMPILE CHATTST:PLNC,"CHATTST:LIST","CHATTST"
EXIT

@cc --- link: the PROGRAM first, then what satisfies it -----------------------
@cc LIST-ENTRIES-UNDEFINED is the check that every name crossed the BRF
@cc boundary. A name longer than SEVEN characters, or one that collides with
@cc another in its first seven, shows up there and NOWHERE else.
@BRF-LINKER-C01
PROGRAM-FILE "CHATTS"
LOAD CHATTST
LOAD CHATLIB
LIBRARY-MODE ON
LOAD PLANC-1BANK-F00
LIST-ENTRIES-UNDEFINED
EXIT

@cc ===========================================================================
@cc Built CHATTS:PROG. Run it with @CHATTS
@cc
@cc Every line starts PASS or FAIL and the last line is a count. One FAIL means
@cc the codec is wrong - do not build the real product until it is clean.
@cc
@cc CHECK BOTH LISTINGS for "*** ERROR" before believing any of it:
@cc   tools\nd-build.ps1 -GateOnly -Listing <pulled CHATLIB:LIST>
@cc ===========================================================================
